  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_016_ClockSkew
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-016
  title: Every card is declined but the terminal looks fine
  category: 0
  content: "Card authorization runs over a secure connection, and secure connections
    check the machine's clock. If Windows has drifted far enough, the processor rejects
    the handshake and every card comes back declined \u2014 while Wi-Fi, IP and POS
    registration all read perfectly correct.\nSo when the terminal is on the store's
    own network (rules out KB-006) with its current IP registered (rules out KB-007)
    and cards still fail, go to System \u25B8 Health and check the clock. Cash still
    working while cards do not is the giveaway: the register is fine, the connection
    to the processor is not."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P16
